From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: one window per Mac display

In full screen every other Mac display gets a full-screen window (its own
Space) showing the next virtio-gpu output, at that display's size, scale and
refresh rate; displays plugged in or out come and go live, and leaving full
screen closes them. The guest agrees and says where its outputs are over the
virtio port org.omacvm.display (socket at OMACVM_DISPLAY_SOCKET); the one
virtio tablet then points into the right output. OMACVM_TEST_SKIP_DISPLAYS and
OMACVM_TEST_MAIN_DISPLAY test it on virtual displays without full screen
or focus. Applies after omacvm-cocoa-window-size.patch.

